  <div class="about-grid record-how">
    <h2 class="about-how-title">How the Record works.</h2>
    <details class="about-principle" name="about-principles"><summary><span class="about-principle-number">01</span><h3>Start with a question.</h3><span class="about-principle-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="about-principle-body">
      <p>
        Each question gathers positions into shared ground, different views, and
        what remains open. The map shows disagreement without forcing a single
        conclusion.
      </p>
    </div></details>
    <details class="about-principle" name="about-principles"><summary><span class="about-principle-number">02</span><h3>Check the source.</h3><span class="about-principle-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="about-principle-body">
      <p>
        Every published position links to the speaker, timestamp, surrounding
        exchange, and original recording so readers can inspect the record
        themselves.
      </p>
    </div></details>
    <details class="about-principle" name="about-principles"><summary><span class="about-principle-number">03</span><h3>Challenge the map.</h3><span class="about-principle-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="about-principle-body">
      <p>
        CIF welcomes corrections, missing evidence, and competing
        interpretations. Substantive corrections will remain visible in the
        Record’s change history.
      </p>
    </div></details>
    <details class="about-principle" name="about-principles"><summary><span class="about-principle-number">04</span><h3>Public by default.</h3><span class="about-principle-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="about-principle-body">
      <p>
        No paywall, required email, or institutional affiliation. If
        institutions later help fund, host, or extend the work, access will
        remain public.
      </p>
    </div></details>
  </div>
